## observations (not defects of the checks above)
  - widget bootstrap POSTs per page load (…/api/widget/<key>/bootstrap, all 200): c1440 26/13, c1024 24/13, c768 24/13, c390 22/13, c375 24/13, w390 2/2 — Chromium usually sends TWO per page view (hello on iframe load + on shell ready), WebKit one. They spend the visitor's 10-per-60 s budget that chat shares, so about 5 page views inside one minute can exhaust it. This QA paced page loads to ≤ 4 per 65 s for that reason; no 429 was received.
  - Chromium console WARNINGS (not errors): “The resource …/assets/33888d63a7dbd1775c78.jpg / 609e7b56f7660f5d1f9d.jpg was preloaded using link preload but not used within a few seconds” on detail pages and /contact — hero images of / and /portfolio preloaded as a side effect of route prefetch. Counts per viewport: c1440 18, c1024 23, c768 10, c390 5, c375 7, w390 0.
  - <meta name="robots" content="noindex"> is present on the pages (recorded, not judged).
  - Lazy <img> elements that were never requested in place (hidden gallery tabs on detail pages; the 4th card of each horizontal track on / in WebKit) are counted as “pending”, not broken; each distinct source was loaded through new Image() in the same page and all of them decoded.
  - WebKit first run (superseded, kept as partial/w390.first-run-fast-scroll.json): scrolled through / at Chromium pace, 10 lazy images were still pending and 4 new Image() probes timed out at 15 s; with 300 px / 350 ms steps (settle-slow.js) 13/15 load in place and 15/15 through new Image(), reproduced in a separate probe. Treated as a scroll-pace artifact of the test, not a site defect.

